  "narrative": {
    "intro": "L3 Technologies obligated $348M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company won 228 awards, with an average award size of $1.5M. Obligations fell 39.0% year over year. The Department of Defense supplied most of the business, obligating $308M, and the General Services Administration followed with $39.7M. Research and Development in Biotechnology (except Nanobiotechnology) is the largest market by obligations at $118M. Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing accounted for $71.8M, and Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing accounted for $59M. Engineering Services totaled $56.1M. The FY26 total is part of a multiyear pattern that includes $466M in FY21, $227M in FY22, $451M in FY23, $613M in FY24, and $570M in FY25.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying from L3 Technologies?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $308M in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration is the next-largest buyer, obligating $39.7M. Other agencies are not shown in the top-two list provided."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are L3 Technologies' biggest product and service markets?",
        "body": "Research and Development in Biotechnology (except Nanobiotechnology) is the largest market at $118M. Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing is $71.8M, Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing is $59M, and Engineering Services is $56.1M. Smaller markets include Aircraft Manufacturing at $8.3M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $897K."
      }
    ]
